<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Miyagi Prefecture</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Miyagi Prefecture is a prefecture in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tohoku-region">Tōhoku region</a> of north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/honshu">Honshu</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sendai">Sendai</a>. It was formed after the abolition of the domains in 1871, largely from the lands of the Sendai Domain. Its coast was devastated by the earthquake and tsunami of March 2011.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/miyagi-prefecture.jpg" alt="Miyagi Prefecture" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 663highland · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:211030_Saigyo_Modoshi_no_Matsu_Park_Matsushima_Miyagi_pref_Japan01n.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
